SUMMARY:The Cyber-Policy Nexus: HLS Global Policy Program Briefing for Cy
 bersecurity and Global Policy Students
DESCRIPTION:In Washington\, D.C.\, policy is the new perimeter. Join Isak
  Nti-Asare (Co-Director\, Cybersecurity and Global Policy Program) and Ka
 therine Ntiamoah (Director of Policy Engagement) for a targeted "come and
  go" lunch regarding the Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program.  This se
 ssion is designed specifically for students in the Cybersecurity and Glob
 al Policy joint degree. Whether your goal is a residency at CISA\, the De
 partment of Justice\, the NSA\, or a private sector tech policy firm\, th
 is is your chance to see how the D.C. residency functions as a profession
 al launchpad for your technical expertise.What to Expect:The Cyber Pipeli
 ne: Guidance on identifying and securing D.C. internship placements that 
 value the Luddy/HLS joint-degree background.    Day 1 Readiness: How our 
 "tradecraft" model prepares you to brief officials on complex cyber threa
 ts from your first day in the capital.    The Roadmap: A technical walkth
 rough of the October 15 application deadline and the January 12 start dat
 e for the Spring residency.    Open House Format: We know your schedule i
 s tight. Drop in for 20 minutes to grab lunch and the HLS D.C. Guide\, or
  stay for the full discussion.
