SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Crisis\, Power & P
 olicy Dinner with Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley
DESCRIPTION:Inside the Room Where Geopolitics Happens  How do you go from
  starting out in global affairs to shaping U.S. cyber strategy\, directin
 g counterterrorism operations\, and advising the Pentagon\, White House\,
  and Senate?  Join the Global Competencies Skills Development Series for 
 an intimate\, off-the-record style session with Ambassador Gina Abercromb
 ie-Winstanley—30-year Foreign Service veteran\, former U.S. Ambassador 
 to Malta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council.  No scripted 
 presentations or generic advice—just real tradecraft from someone who h
 as managed war-zone evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest 
 levels of national security.  Who Can Attend?  Open to all: Students (Und
 ergrad &amp\; Grad)\, Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. (Catered dinner p
 rovided)  What You'll Get Out of It      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, smal
 l-group face time with a senior diplomat who operated across the State De
 partment\, Defense Department\, and National Security Council.          C
 risis Tradecraft: Real-world lessons on high-pressure decision-making\, f
 rom counterterrorism networks to cyber warfare and emergency evacuations.
           Insider Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking into n
 ational security\, intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top international 
 fellowships.          Raw Answers: Bring your real questions about power 
 dynamics\, navigating federal bureaucracy\, and building leverage early i
 n your career.      Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley  Ambassad
 or Gina Abercrombie-Winstanley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambass
 ador to the Republic of Malta\, and President of the Middle East Policy C
 ouncil. Her career spans executive leadership roles across the Department
  of State\, Defense Department\, National Security Council\, and Senate F
 oreign Relations Committee. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber f
 orces on foreign policy priorities\, expanded international counterterror
 ism partnerships as Deputy Coordinator for Counterterrorism\, and led the
  emergency evacuation of thousands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She 
 is a recipient of the State Department Superior Honor Award for acts of c
 ourage during an al-Qaeda attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.
